The FlowXer source code in this repository is Apache-2.0. That matches the
Media eXchange Layer (MXL) project it integrates with. The published Docker
images additionally bundle third-party media libraries that remain under their
own licenses; shipping those binaries does not relicense FlowXer itself.


Third-party components
======================

Apache-2.0
  Media eXchange Layer (MXL) — https://github.com/dmf-mxl/mxl
    Built into the mixer image (libmxl, used by the media engine).
  FastAPI, Starlette, Pydantic, Uvicorn
  The media engine (engine/) adapts parts of mxl-multiviewer
  (https://github.com/LeeO86/mxl-multiviewer, Apache-2.0); see engine/NOTICE.

MIT
  React, React DOM, Vite (operator GUI)
  MediaMTX — https://github.com/bluenviron/mediamtx (bundled in the mixer image)
  mxl-webrtc-monitor — https://github.com/LeeO86/mxl-webrtc-monitor
    Copyright (c) 2026 Adrian Hilber (MIT): the engine's MediaMTX and NVENC settings.
  Concepts and conversion/loop-conform semantics adapted from
  mxl-test-player — https://github.com/LeeO86/mxl-test-player
  Copyright (c) 2026 Adrian Hilber (MIT). FlowXer reimplements the
  ideas; no C++ sources were copied.

LGPL-2.1+
  FFmpeg / libav via the Ubuntu ffmpeg packages (mixer image)

NVIDIA CUDA EULA
  The CUDA runtime, linked statically into the media engine

Other
  nginx (gui image) — 2-clause BSD

Source for the packaged libraries is available from the Ubuntu archive and from
the upstream projects listed above.
